00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.640
Forehand slice lesson.

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:04.850
The forehand slice.

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:09.430
In a tennis match the forehand slice is generally not a regular baseline shot.

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:12.510
It mostly shows up when you're stretched to save a ball, or now and then to change the rhythm.

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:18.100
We pick out a few key points for you to try and feel in real play.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:22.560
Again a continental grip; the wrist of the racket hand is cocked up and firm, the left hand holds the throat.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:27.280
Facing the ball, open the elbow and the racket face, take it back with the body to six o'clock and step in.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:30.220
When you hit, your weight moves from back to front.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:36.500
At contact the racket face is still upright: drive through the back of the ball, don't slice underneath it.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:39.900
That makes a heavy slice that dips on your opponent.

